  [plan] action=answer paper='' queries=[]
         reasoning='We have excerpts from all three named papers in their own files, so enough information to compare them. Smoothing a Program Soundly and Robustly makes numerical optimization work by replacing a program’s discontinuous semantics with a Gaussian-smoothed semantic function, enabling gradient-based search and iterative optimization over decreasing β values. Euler uses that smooth-interpretation machinery as its core algorithm: it compiles a sketch with holes into an executable, then repeatedly optimizes the smoothed program while lowering β to refine the solution. ReaS makes numerical optimization work by making programs end-to-end differentiable: it smooths Boolean conditionals, relaxes Boolean unknowns to reals, applies automatic differentiation/SNOPT-style optimization, and uses SAT solving to fix Boolean choices and escape local minima.'
